  "Comments": "Vapor pressure fitted to the NIST WebBook Antoine equation of Stull (1947), 254.8 to 394 K; the Henry constant and infinite dilution activity coefficient of Fenclova et al. (2014) imply a pressure 21 % lower at 25 C (to be checked), within 0.9 %. Normal boiling point 394.4 K from that curve. Tc, Pc and the ideal gas formation enthalpy and Gibbs energy by Joback (1987) from that boiling point, acentric factor by Lee-Kesler. Heat of vaporization from the slope of the vapor pressure curve (36.2 kJ/mol at the boiling point), carried with Watson's exponent. Heat capacities, transport properties and surface tension of N-butyl acetate (ChemSep), per unit mass. Liquid density 879 kg/m3 at 20 C (to be checked). UNIFAC groups approximate. Its volatility from water in a juice comes from the Henry constant of the juice package.",
